// General Concept:
// After budget(Refer Budget Model) creation, we allocate budget to categories(Refer categories model). Now after allocating budget to categories, we purchase resources
// for the categories(Refer Purchase Order Model ). For this purpose we create purchase order.
// Purchase Order in simple terms is a contract that is created for purchasing the items from a vendor

// Initally a purchase order can be created as draft or it can be directly sent for approval
// When purchase order is created as a draft we have the option to cancel the purchase order.

// When send/resend purchase order for approval, that total amount for the purchase order gets deducted from the lineitems.
// When the purchase order is rejected/ reconsidered, that total amount for the purchase order gets added back to the lineitems

// Note: For understanding all the amounts related to the purchase order please refer function  addPoAmounts (path  - src\utils\misc2.js) after reading field definitions

// Short Closing Purchase Order - After the purchase order is fully approved, the user might want to prematurely close down the contract because of some reason
//                                We can either short close some item or all the items for a purchase order. When an po or po item is short close, the corresponding amount
//                                is added back to the respective lineitems

//                                1. To understand how short close works please refer api /v1/finance-service/purchase-order/short-close-po/:id
//                                2. To understand how short close of po item works please refer api /v1/finance-service/purchase-order/short-close-po-item/:id

// We also track the advance that we pay to vendor after the purchase order is fully approved.
// After the purchase order is fully approved, and while creating the purchase order, the creator of the purchase order has entered advance percentage(advance.advancePercentage)
// then Advance Payment can be initiated on the purchase order.

// Note: 1. After the purchase order is fully approved, we can can do both Initiate Advance Payment and create GRNs for the purchase order. But advance cannot be initiated on the purchase order for which grn is created
//       2. Advance payment cannot be initiated for the purchase orders where the amount is less than or equal to zero

